    "lawCode": "Add §1202-ll, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7820A\n\nSPONSOR: OBERACKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the town of\nGardiner to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal\nof such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Town of Gardiner to authorize and empowered to adopt\nand amend local laws imposing a hotel and motel tax. Each enactment of\nsuch a local law may provide for the imposition of a hotel or motel tax\nfor a period of time no-longer than two (2) years from the date of its\nenactment. Nothing in this section shall prohibit the adoption and\nenactment of local laws pursuant to the provisions of this section, upon\nexpiration of any other local law adopted pursuant to this section.\n\nThe rate of such tax shall not exceed five (5%) percent of the per diem\nrental rate for each room, provided however, that such tax shall not be\napplicable to a permanent resident of a hotel or motel.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. The tax law is amended by adding a new section 1202-11.\n\nSection 2. This act shall take effect immediately and shall expire after\ntwo years.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nAmendment to the NYS Tax law by adding section 1202-11.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of Gardiner provides essential municipal services, infrastruc-\nture maintenance and public safety initiatives that benefit both resi-\ndents and visitors; and\n\nTourism and overnight lodging contribute significantly to the local\neconomy, increasing the demand for municipal services; and\n\nA hotel or motel occupancy tax would provide a dedicated revenue source\nto help support these services without imposing additional burdens on\nlocal taxpayers; and\n\nThe authority to impose such a tax requires specific enabling legis-\nlation from the New York State legislature; and\n\nSimilar occupancy taxes have been successfully implemented in other New\nYork municipalities, providing additional revenue for essential\nservices; and\n\nThis legislation is sought so that the Town of Gardiner can collect the\noccupancy tax in addition to any other tax authorized and imposed. The\nrate of such tax shall not exceed five (5%) percent of the per diem\nrental rate for each room, provided however, that such tax shall not be\napplicable to a permanent resident of a hotel or motel.\nRequested by the Town of Gardiner Town Board by resolution adopted on\nFebruary 10, 2026.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire after two years\n",
